cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  DORA-as-Code: A Comparative Evaluation of Policy-as-Code Tools
  for Automated EU Regulatory Compliance in GitOps-Managed
  Kubernetes Environments
message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying data, please cite
  both the dissertation and this repository.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mohit Kumar
    family-names: Somashekar
    email: a00047340@mytudublin.ie
    affiliation: >-
      School of Enterprise Computing and Digital Transformation,
      Technological University Dublin, Tallaght Campus
repository-code: https://github.com/mo-it/dora-as-code
license: MIT
version: 1.0-dissertation
date-released: '2026-08-22'
keywords:
  - DORA
  - policy-as-code
  - GitOps
  - Kubernetes
  - Kyverno
  - OPA Gatekeeper
  - admission control
  - regulatory compliance
  - DevSecOps
abstract: >-
  Research artefacts accompanying an MSc DevOps dissertation that
  maps EU Digital Operational Resilience Act (Regulation (EU)
  2022/2554) ICT risk management requirements from Articles 5 to 15
  onto executable Kubernetes admission policies, and compares
  Kyverno and OPA Gatekeeper enforcing them within an ArgoCD GitOps
  pipeline. The repository contains a 30-entry DORA requirements
  register, 25 policies implemented in each engine, a generated
  ground-truth test suite, a randomised complete block performance
  benchmark, a compliance evidence hook, and the analysis tooling
  needed to reproduce every reported result.
references:
  - type: legislation
    title: >-
      Regulation (EU) 2022/2554 on digital operational resilience
      for the financial sector (DORA)
    authors:
      - name: European Parliament and Council of the European Union
    year: 2022
    url: https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2022/2554/oj
